1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 1. James Lockwood .  General Notes: 1. Name is from the details of the 2nd marriage of his son, Justus Bush Lockwood, in Bergen, Norway in 1834. 2. Several trees at ancestry.com have Justus as being born on 13th Ma
2 CONC rch 1784 in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania. However no source information has been supplied by any tree. In the 1790 census, there is only one Lockwood family in Philadelphia:- James Lockwood & Co, Merchant at Water Street, East Side,
2 CONC  Philadelphia, Pennsylvania. The household consists of:- Males under 16:- 3 Males over 16:- 2 Females:- 5 There are no Lockwoods in Pennsylvania in the 1800 census. In the 1810 census there are two Lockwood families in Pennsylvani
2 CONC a both in Philadelphia:- (a) Clover Lockwood - 5 persons (b) Laetitia Lockwood - 2 persons 3. In a Rootsweb posting dated 5th April 1998 from Marcia Green, she lists:-
2 CONT
2 CONT Names of Foreigners Who Took the Oath of Allegiance to the Province and State of Pennsylvania: Volume 2 A HISTORY OF THE TEST LAWS AND LAWS CONCERNING OATHS OF ALLEGIANCE IN FORCE IN PENNSYLVANIA BETWEEN JUNE 13, 1777, AND MARCH 1
2 CONC 3, 1789.
2 CONT
2 CONT JAMES LOCKWOOD, a native of Connecticut, a resident here near two years. Mercht. 4. The "Edmonds Family File" at ancestry.com states that "HE WAS THE SON OF BRIGADIER MAJOR JAMES LOCKWOOD 1746-1795 AND ELIZABETH"
2 CONT
2 CONT James married someone.  His child was:
2 CONT
2 CONT + 2 M    i. Justus Bush Lockwood was born about 1784 in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, USA and died on 25 Aug 1839 in Bergen, Hordaland, Norway aged about 55. 
2 CONT
